README Must Include
Your README should clearly explain:
  1.   Project title
  2.   Domain selected
  3.   Business problem
  4.   Dataset details
  5.   Base model used
  6.   Non-instruction fine-tuning approach
  7.   Instruction fine-tuning approach
  8.   DPO alignment approach
  9.   LoRA / QLoRA configuration
  10.   Training screenshots or logs
  11.   Before vs after output comparison
  12.   Final observations
  13.   Challenges faced
  14.   Future improvements

Public Dataset References
Students can either create their own dataset or use public datasets from Hugging Face, Kaggle, or public documents.
Before using any dataset, students must:
  oo   Check the dataset license
  oo   Clean the dataset
  oo   Verify the quality
  oo   Convert it into the required format

Customer Support Assistant
https://huggingface.co/datasets/bitext/Bitext-customer-support-llm-chatbot-training-dataset

Finance / Banking FAQ Assistant
https://huggingface.co/datasets/PolyAI/banking77

Healthcare FAQ Assistant
https://huggingface.co/datasets/medalpaca/medical_meadow_medical_flashcards

Legal Document FAQ Assistant
https://www.atticusprojectai.org/cuad
https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.06268

Course Doubt Assistant / General Q&A
https://huggingface.co/datasets/toughdata/quora-question-answer-dataset

E-commerce Product Support Assistant
https://huggingface.co/datasets/bitext/Bitext-customer-support-llm-chatbot-training-dataset
https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.04364

IT Helpdesk Assistant
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/suraj520/customer-support-ticket-dataset
https://huggingface.co/datasets/Tobi-Bueck/customer-support-tickets

HR Policy Assistant
Ready-made HR fine-tuning datasets are limited. The best approach is to use a public employee handbook or HR policy PDF and generate Q&A pairs from it.

Final Expected Output
By the end of this assignment, you should have a working domain-specific fine-tuned LLM that has gone through:
  1.   Non-instruction fine-tuning
  2.   Instruction fine-tuning
  3.   DPO preference alignment
This project should be good enough to explain in interviews as:
I created a domain-specific AI assistant using Unsloth. I first performed non-instruction fine-tuning on raw domain text, then instruction fine-tuning on Q&A data, and finally DPO alignment using preference data. I compared the base model, SFT model, and DPO-aligned model and built a simple inference script.


